===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gel-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|gélatine||jelly, gel}}, from {{der|en|it|gelatina||jelly, gel}}, from {{m|it|gelare||to freeze}}, from {{der|en|la|gelare||to freeze}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɛlətɪn/}} or sometimes {{IPAchar|/ˈd͡ʒɛlətiːn/|lang=en}}; also {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɛləʔ.n̩/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-gelatin.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[protein]] derived through partial [[hydrolysis]] of the [[collagen]] extracted from [[animal]] [[skin]], [[bone]]s, [[cartilage]], [[ligament]]s, etc.
# An [[edible]] [[jelly]] made from this material.
# A thin, [[translucent]] [[membrane]] used as a [[filter]] for photography or for [[theatrical]] [[lighting]] [[effect]]s.
